It is Saturday afternoon, and I am coming home from the café.
Mostly I am a little tired after the shift.
I walk up the stairs to my flat.
A small card is stuck to my door.
It is a notification from the post.
I take the card off and read it.
The language is very official.
It says: "Your shipment will be deposited in the parcel shop."
I read the text twice.
In which parcel shop exactly?
Normally the address is at the bottom of the card.
Ah, here it is.
The shop is right around the corner.
And until when can I pick it up?
I read the next sentence.
"Your parcel will be kept for seven working days."
Very good, then I do not have to hurry today.
I put the card in my trouser pocket.
I will simply pick up the parcel on Monday.
Now I unlock the door and look forward to my sofa.
